Package: scx-scheds
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: sched_ext schedulers and tools
 sched_ext is a Linux kernel feature that lets CPU schedulers be written
 as BPF programs and loaded at runtime, without rebuilding the kernel.
 It needs a kernel built with CONFIG_SCHED_CLASS_EXT.
 .
 This package contains the schedulers from the sched-ext/scx project,
 including scx_bpfland, scx_cosmos, scx_flash, scx_lavd, scx_layered,
 scx_p2dq, scx_rustland and scx_rusty, plus the scxtop monitoring tool.
